Defects found:

- **Idempotency guard satisfied by its own marker/comment**: lines 32 and 37.  
  Input: `check("<!-- Generator build <code>abcdef1</code> -->")` returns `PASS`.  
  Consequence: an invisible HTML comment satisfies a reader-facing build-stamp gate.

- **Instrument reading a different binding than the match**: line 34.  
  Input: `check("x"*801 + "<p>generator build <code>abcdef1</code></p>")` returns `FAIL`.  
  Consequence: `STAMP` accepts the lowercase marker, but the segment reader uses a separate case-sensitive `find()` and ignores the actual stamp.

- **Instrument reading a different field than the stamp**: line 37.  
  Input: `check("<p><code>abcdef1</code></p><p>Generator build (none)</p>")` returns `PASS`.  
  Consequence: an unrelated nearby `<code>` value is accepted as the generator commit.

- **Selector not scoped to the stamp**: line 35.  
  Input: `check("<p>Generator build <code>abcdef1</code></p><p>UNKNOWN endpoint status</p>")` returns `FAIL`.  
  Consequence: unrelated `UNKNOWN` text near a valid stamp makes the page fail.

- **Selector not scoped to the stamp**: line 40.  
  Input: `check("<p>Generator build <code>abcdef1</code></p><p>NOT REPRODUCIBLE claim elsewhere</p>")` returns `PASS` with dirty-tree wording.  
  Consequence: dirty status is attributed to the build stamp from unrelated page text.

